WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.740
Governments decide whether
to build new roads,

2
00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:05.300
railways and flood defences.

3
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:09.200
A new road brings faster
journeys and fewer crashes.

4
00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.150
It also brings noise
to the homes beside it.

5
00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:15.660
Nobody sells quiet or clean air in a shop.

6
00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:17.810
So how do they get into the sums?

7
00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:20.090
How can a government
put a price on cleaner

8
00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:23.240
air before deciding
whether to build a road?

9
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:26.460
In this mission, you'll open
the toolkit economists use

10
00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:29.470
to value things that are
never bought or sold.

11
00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:32.160
Then you'll set a pollution tax yourself,

12
00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:35.810
and see what happens when the
estimate behind it is wrong.

13
00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:38.560
Your mission: find out
how a money value is

14
00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.910
put on things that have no price.
